WEBVTT

00:02.309 --> 00:05.745
<i>It seems today that all you see</i>

00:05.846 --> 00:09.044
<i>Is violence in movies and sex on TV</i>

00:09.150 --> 00:12.551
<i>But where are those
good old-fashioned values</i>

00:12.654 --> 00:15.623
<i>On which we used to rely?</i>

00:15.723 --> 00:18.887
<i>Lucky there's a family guy</i>

00:18.994 --> 00:22.225
<i>Lucky there's a man who
positively can do</i>

00:22.331 --> 00:23.889
<i>All the things that make us</i>

00:23.999 --> 00:25.591
<i>Laugh and cry</i>

00:25.701 --> 00:30.469
<i>He's a family guy</i>

00:36.047 --> 00:37.571
<i>This Tuesday on Lifetime,</i>

00:37.682 --> 00:40.810
<i>Valerie Bertinelli stars
in a Lifetime original movie.</i>

00:40.918 --> 00:43.614
<i>You know, Doctor, you said
you were going to cure my cancer,</i>

00:43.721 --> 00:45.348
<i>but all you did was rape me.</i>

00:45.456 --> 00:47.482
<i>I'm starting to think
I don't have cancer at all.</i>

00:47.592 --> 00:51.460
<i>Well, you're right, about the rape part,
but I'm sorry, you still do have cancer.</i>

00:53.765 --> 00:55.358
<i>Valerie Bertinelli in...</i>

00:59.205 --> 01:03.266
Brian, did you know that
Daryl Hannah has one wooden finger?

01:03.376 --> 01:06.471
<i>- Really? Where did you read that?
- In People magazine.</i>

01:07.681 --> 01:09.979
Jillian, can you run
and get me a beer from the kitchen?

01:10.084 --> 01:11.745
Oh, yeah, sure, no problem.

01:11.852 --> 01:14.116
Hey, Jillian, you and Brian
got big plans tonight?

01:14.221 --> 01:16.918
<i>Yeah. Brian's taking me to Disney On Ice.</i>

01:18.126 --> 01:19.650
I want to go.

01:19.761 --> 01:22.059
Well, Peter, if you want,
you can have my ticket.

01:22.163 --> 01:25.099
What?
But, Brian, I thought you wanted to go.

01:25.201 --> 01:28.637
Stitch is going to do a skating duet
with Sebastian, the crab.

01:29.839 --> 01:31.397
It's not really my cup of tea.

01:31.507 --> 01:34.204
Plus, Walt Disney was
an outspoken anti-Semite.

01:34.311 --> 01:39.112
So, Disney, ABC, ESPN, Touchstone...
These would all be things to avoid.

01:39.216 --> 01:43.984
<i>Well, oh, okay.
Peter, you want to go see Disney On Ice?</i>

01:48.726 --> 01:50.216
Oh, God, yes!

01:50.328 --> 01:53.787
I'll be right back. I'm going to go
put on my Donald Duck costume.

01:54.633 --> 01:55.861
Ready.

02:01.206 --> 02:04.540
Meg, lend me 25 cents
so I can ride the toy airplane outside

02:04.644 --> 02:06.635
and make the immigrant kids jealous.

02:08.581 --> 02:11.448
Look at me.
I'm having a magical aerial adventure

02:11.551 --> 02:14.749
because my family has disposable income.
Here you go.

02:14.855 --> 02:17.983
- What is this?
- It's a pamphlet on why I'm bombing you.

02:18.592 --> 02:19.991
- Hey, Meg.
- Hi, Carl.

02:20.094 --> 02:21.527
Hey, how come
you're always here by yourself?

02:21.630 --> 02:23.154
Are you, like, a bitch or something?

02:23.265 --> 02:25.460
- No, I have friends.
- Oh.

02:25.567 --> 02:27.535
Well, you should bring some of them
in here.

02:27.636 --> 02:29.570
- Any of them have braces?
- Yeah.

02:29.671 --> 02:33.130
I love braces. My mom has them.

02:33.810 --> 02:38.042
Well, listen... I need disposable diapers,
but it looks like you're out.

02:38.147 --> 02:40.946
Oh, no, I got some in the stockroom.
Hang on.

02:41.051 --> 02:43.576
<i>Oh, Vince Vaughn's on the cover
of Entertainment Weekly.</i>

02:43.687 --> 02:45.917
Here's my summary
of every Vince Vaughn movie.

02:46.023 --> 02:48.150
"Oh, I'm incapable of loving
another person.

02:48.258 --> 02:50.226
"Oh, wait, no, I'm not. The end."

02:50.327 --> 02:53.058
I don't even want to look at his face.

02:53.598 --> 02:55.566
Stewie, what the hell are you doing?

02:55.667 --> 02:59.125
Oh, my God!
Now, I've got to clean all this up.

03:01.240 --> 03:02.867
Carl, I'm so sorry.

03:02.975 --> 03:05.967
Wow, Meg,
you alphabetized all the magazines.

03:06.078 --> 03:10.413
- Hey, you want a job?
- What? Me? Here? Yeah, sure.

03:10.517 --> 03:11.814
Great. You start tomorrow.

03:16.356 --> 03:18.085
- Hey, Chris.
- Hey, Meg.

03:18.925 --> 03:20.052
I don't have any money,

03:20.161 --> 03:23.562
so I'm going to have to pay
for these comic books with my poo.

03:23.664 --> 03:25.154
Chris, how come
you don't have any money?

03:25.266 --> 03:26.426
I thought you had a paper route.

03:26.534 --> 03:29.868
Well, I'm taking a sabbatical
to focus on my pottery.

03:29.972 --> 03:33.874
- Oh. How's that working out?
- Not good, Meg, not good.

03:33.976 --> 03:36.809
Well, maybe I could talk to Carl
and get you a job here.

03:36.912 --> 03:40.815
- You could do that?
- Absolutely. Carl totally trusts me.

03:40.917 --> 03:45.149
You and I will be the best brother-sister
team since Maggie and Jake Gyllenhaal.

03:45.455 --> 03:48.448
- I'm more off-putting.
- No, I'm more off-putting.

03:48.559 --> 03:50.959
I'm more unattractive to put in a lead role.

03:51.061 --> 03:55.157
- Well, I'm a bigger box office drag.
- Kids, kids. You're both...

03:55.266 --> 03:56.597
Just awful.

03:59.938 --> 04:00.962
Oh, hi, Brian.

04:01.072 --> 04:02.972
I thought you were
spending the day with Jillian.

04:03.074 --> 04:05.372
I was, but Peter took her off my hands.

04:05.477 --> 04:08.038
Perfect timing.
I've been feeling a little smothered lately.

04:08.147 --> 04:10.411
Plus, it's given me a chance
to work on my novel.

04:10.516 --> 04:13.417
- And I finally have a title.
- Oh, what is it?

04:13.519 --> 04:16.249
"Faster Than the Speed of Love."

04:19.726 --> 04:21.887
That is the worst title I've ever heard.

04:21.995 --> 04:24.964
No, it's the story of a boy
who has to rescue his father,

04:25.065 --> 04:28.524
who's a pilot that's been taken captive
by a militant Islamic country.

04:29.971 --> 04:31.939
<i>That's the movie Iron Eagle.</i>

04:32.040 --> 04:35.498
What? Is that... Is that a recent film?

04:35.944 --> 04:38.140
They made three sequels!

04:38.247 --> 04:41.683
Yeah, well, in mine, the boy's got to
gather all these old World War II pilots

04:41.784 --> 04:43.979
to help him rescue his father.

04:44.086 --> 04:46.783
That's one of the sequels!

04:48.358 --> 04:51.623
Well, well, in mine,
one of the World War II guys is Japanese,

04:51.728 --> 04:53.423
but they accept him anyway.

04:54.965 --> 04:57.196
I'm going to pee in my pants!

04:59.904 --> 05:02.930
Boy, it sure is fun
hanging out with you, Peter.

05:05.677 --> 05:08.271
That means "thank you"
in my new language I'm inventing.

05:09.715 --> 05:11.945
Anyway, all I was saying is,
if you think about it,

05:12.050 --> 05:14.245
<i>it shouldn't have been
Ferris Bueller's Day Off.</i>

05:14.353 --> 05:16.822
<i>It should've been Ferris Bueller's Day On,</i>

05:16.923 --> 05:18.686
'cause that was all the stuff
he wanted to do.

05:18.791 --> 05:23.751
Yeah! And he was so on that day,
so it kind of works on two levels.

05:23.863 --> 05:26.924
Well, I don't know what you mean by that,
but how about that Cameron, huh?

05:27.034 --> 05:29.264
- Oh, definitely.
- Am I right?

05:29.370 --> 05:31.133
It was his day off, too.

05:31.238 --> 05:33.229
That is just what I was going to...
His day off...

05:33.340 --> 05:34.933
That is just what I was going to say.

05:35.043 --> 05:37.534
You know, you are a catch, young lady.
You know that?

05:37.645 --> 05:41.274
I don't know when the hell Brian is going
to open his eyes and get serious with you.

05:42.484 --> 05:43.850
I really wish he would.

05:43.953 --> 05:47.047
It'd be so great
if we were at least living together.

05:47.156 --> 05:49.386
Well, you need to
just lay it on the line with him.

05:49.492 --> 05:51.551
Either he commits to you, or you're gone.

05:51.761 --> 05:53.992
What the hell did you do?

05:54.097 --> 05:56.998
Because of what you said,
Jillian wants us to move in together!

05:57.100 --> 05:59.864
Well, I think you should, Brian.
She's beautiful, she's funny,

05:59.970 --> 06:02.599
and she is smart as the day is wide.

06:02.707 --> 06:04.937
Don't you understand? I don't want
a committed relationship with Jillian.

06:06.720 --> 06:09.883
Well, it sounds like she does.
And if you're never going to get serious,

06:09.990 --> 06:11.685
then you're not being fair to her.

06:11.792 --> 06:13.158
I mean, what are you, Brian?

06:13.261 --> 06:16.424
One of those creepy guys
who just uses a woman for sex?

06:16.531 --> 06:18.556
Because Jillian deserves better.

06:18.667 --> 06:20.828
She has feelings, you know,

06:20.935 --> 06:24.030
and she's devoted a lot of time
and energy to this relationship

06:24.140 --> 06:28.133
with some expectation that it could grow
into something much more significant,

06:28.244 --> 06:30.838
and if you're just stringing her along,

06:30.946 --> 06:34.110
well, then I got to say,
I have lost a lot of respect for you, Brian.

06:34.217 --> 06:36.048
You don't really think
I'm like that, do you?

06:36.153 --> 06:38.951
- Prove me wrong.
- All right, I will, Lois.

06:39.056 --> 06:42.754
I will ask her to move in with me,
and you'll see, I've got what it takes.

06:42.860 --> 06:44.020
See, that wasn't so bad, was it?

06:45.229 --> 06:47.424
I got to say, that was fantastic.

06:47.532 --> 06:49.966
What do you say, we go back
to your place for round two?

06:50.068 --> 06:51.400
Sounds good to me.

06:54.006 --> 06:57.874
Wow, three times in a row.
You're amazing, Glenn.

06:57.976 --> 07:00.035
Well, I just take a lot of pride
in what I do.

07:00.146 --> 07:02.512
Hey, what's going on here?

07:03.717 --> 07:06.345
- Get off my wife!
- Oh, my God, oh, my God!

07:07.987 --> 07:10.786
You shot my Homie!
I'm calling the police!

07:12.093 --> 07:13.117
<i>Ay Caramba!</i>

07:13.227 --> 07:14.694
Mum and Dad are dead!

07:15.896 --> 07:19.424
Oh, no, who will pay
for my saxophone lessons?

07:33.282 --> 07:37.048
Boy, you know, I got to tell you, Jillian,
this move is really working out great.

07:37.153 --> 07:41.113
- It just feels right, you know.
- Cool. Rock on, Brian.

07:41.225 --> 07:42.351
Okay, done.

07:45.562 --> 07:47.029
Stewie. Hey. What's up?

07:47.131 --> 07:49.293
Oh, I was just on my way
back from the cobbler.

07:49.434 --> 07:51.925
Figured before I stopped
by the apothecary, I'd come here,

07:52.036 --> 07:54.163
and then it's off to the haberdasher.

07:54.272 --> 07:57.105
These turn of the century business jokes
doing anything for you?

07:57.208 --> 07:59.040
- Not really.
- Did you use the jokes?

07:59.145 --> 08:01.010
Yeah, they're not landing.

08:02.448 --> 08:06.179
- Got your mail. So, how's it going?
- I tell you, Stewie, it's going great.

08:06.285 --> 08:08.948
And that's the worst part.
I can't afford the rent.

08:09.055 --> 08:11.148
I'll be lucky if I can make it
to the end of the month.

08:11.258 --> 08:13.249
Sounds like you need a roommate.

08:13.360 --> 08:14.987
- Where did you get that kind of money?
- I picked up Chris's paper route.

08:19.659 --> 08:23.823
Oh, OshKosh B'Gosh,
it's a brand new paperboy.

08:23.930 --> 08:25.921
That's a mighty full sack you're carrying.

08:26.032 --> 08:29.833
- Piss off, you perverted old freak!
- Oh, we got a fighter.

08:33.440 --> 08:35.738
Wow, you were almost in a dirt bike race?

08:35.843 --> 08:38.210
Yeah, yeah, I filled out
most of the paperwork, too.

08:38.313 --> 08:41.942
- You are the coolest guy I have ever met.
- Yeah?

08:42.050 --> 08:46.010
Hey, guys. Chris, I need you to
stack the boxes in the back for me.

08:46.455 --> 08:48.650
You know what, Meg?
Why don't you do that?

08:48.757 --> 08:51.817
- I need Chris up here with me.
- But the boxes are really heavy.

08:51.927 --> 08:53.861
Oh, that's 'cause
there's a bunch of stuff in them.

08:54.797 --> 08:55.765
Chris?

08:56.967 --> 08:57.956
Yeah.

08:58.535 --> 09:00.662
<i>Chris, you ever see
the movie Cruel Intentions?</i>

09:00.770 --> 09:01.737
No.

09:01.838 --> 09:05.297
Oh, Selma Blair and Sarah Michelle Gellar
make out. It's pretty hot.

09:06.043 --> 09:07.806
47 minutes, 16 seconds in.

09:07.912 --> 09:09.379
- No way.
- Yeah, yeah.

09:09.480 --> 09:10.640
You know what's another great movie?

09:10.748 --> 09:13.114
<i>Career Opportunities with
Jennifer Connelly.</i>

09:13.217 --> 09:15.413
I mean, that's one of those movies that...

09:15.521 --> 09:19.218
I mean, she's really hot in it,
but it's also a good movie.

09:19.458 --> 09:22.188
<i>She was in A Beautiful Mind,
and I've got to say,</i>

09:22.294 --> 09:26.891
the direction was excellent,
but I was very disappointed that she...

09:27.000 --> 09:29.525
Wore clothes the entire film.

09:29.636 --> 09:31.263
Was she hot in it?

09:31.371 --> 09:35.832
Yeah, in the way that, like,
classy women with expensive clothing

09:35.943 --> 09:38.673
who never take them off are hot,
you know?

09:39.513 --> 09:41.003
- No.
- All right.

09:41.115 --> 09:42.810
So, like, you see a hot girl,

09:42.917 --> 09:45.546
and you're, like, " Okay, I appreciate
your exterior beauty

09:45.654 --> 09:46.951
"'cause you've definitely worked at it

09:47.055 --> 09:50.320
"with the clothing, and the jewelry,
and the makeup and stuff."

09:50.425 --> 09:53.657
But secretly, I'm just, like, " Hey, man...

09:53.763 --> 09:57.130
"Where is the chase
and how do I cut to it?"

09:57.233 --> 09:58.632
Wow, you're smart.

10:00.770 --> 10:02.032
What?

10:05.375 --> 10:08.674
Listen, I hope you don't mind
Stewie staying with us for a little while.

10:08.779 --> 10:11.873
He... He just gets really lonely
without me at home.

10:11.982 --> 10:15.885
You're so fatherly. It really turns me on.

10:17.188 --> 10:20.817
Brian, there's no more
graham crackers.

10:20.925 --> 10:23.793
- They're in the cabinet.
- I don't see them.

10:23.896 --> 10:27.127
They're right in front of you.
Which cabinet are you looking at?

10:27.232 --> 10:30.326
- Can't you just come in here?
- No, I'm busy!

10:32.272 --> 10:36.732
Oh, no! Oh, no, Brian!

10:37.177 --> 10:39.475
Oh, no! Oh, no!

10:39.579 --> 10:42.481
Oh, Brian, we need paper towels!

10:42.583 --> 10:46.451
Oh! Oh, it's going under the fridge! Oh!

10:46.554 --> 10:48.988
- Just use a dish towel!
- There aren't any, Brian!

10:49.090 --> 10:53.357
You need to come in here!
Oh! We are gonna have ants!

10:59.534 --> 11:00.627
A hundred points.

11:00.737 --> 11:02.796
<i>Meg, clean up aisle two.</i>

11:02.905 --> 11:05.499
What the hell is this?
I am not cleaning this up.

11:05.608 --> 11:09.169
- Meg, less talkie, more sweepie.
- Shut up, Chris!

11:09.278 --> 11:10.644
You can't tell me what to do.

11:10.981 --> 11:13.211
Actually, Meg, as your supervisor, he can.

11:13.317 --> 11:15.683
- Supervisor?
- Yeah, I promoted him this morning.

11:15.786 --> 11:17.811
- Promoted me this morning.
- What?

11:17.921 --> 11:20.857
Carl, you promised me
that assistant manager position.

11:21.292 --> 11:22.759
Meg, things change.

11:22.861 --> 11:25.022
<i>Hey, you ever see
Broken Lizard's Club Dread?</i>

11:25.130 --> 11:26.188
No.

11:26.297 --> 11:28.492
Well, go see that movie
and absorb its message,

11:28.600 --> 11:30.694
and you'll get the gist
of what I'm talking about.

11:30.803 --> 11:33.829
- Carl, this isn't fair!
- All right, then, you're fired.

11:33.939 --> 11:37.136
What? But... No, you can't...

11:40.914 --> 11:42.882
Don't worry about it, Chris, she'll be fine.

11:42.983 --> 11:46.885
Hey, by the way, you know who else is hot
in kind of a screwed up way?

11:46.987 --> 11:48.478
Mary Stuart Masterson.

11:48.589 --> 11:51.251
Yeah, yeah, in that sort of
"you think you could get her,

11:51.359 --> 11:53.486
"cause she could be your brother"
kind of thing.

11:53.594 --> 11:56.995
Like, she's gettable, you know?
Like Elisabeth Shue.

11:57.098 --> 11:58.964
- Oh, I remember her.
- Yeah.

11:59.201 --> 12:04.468
<i>You know, she was in Leaving Las Vegas
in addition to Adventures in Babysitting.</i>

12:04.573 --> 12:08.101
One of those underrated actresses
that was always talented and beautiful,

12:08.211 --> 12:10.270
and never quite popped,
if you know the meaning.

12:10.380 --> 12:12.610
- Who, Elisabeth Shue?
- Yeah.

12:12.716 --> 12:16.777
<i>Like totally naked in Leaving Las Vegas.</i>

12:16.986 --> 12:21.014
And still so hot. Like...

12:21.125 --> 12:24.117
- I don't see art films.
- Like, like, crazy hot.

12:24.228 --> 12:27.528
Yeah, it's about 39 minutes, 45 seconds in.

12:27.632 --> 12:29.395
- Oh.
- It's a really exceptional sequence.

12:29.501 --> 12:32.436
I mean, Nick Cage is
poisoning himself with alcohol.

12:32.537 --> 12:35.529
He's a... He's a failed writer
who just decides that,

12:35.640 --> 12:37.666
"Oh, I'm going to have
a big last hurrah in Las Vegas."

12:37.777 --> 12:41.941
And then he meets a whore and pays her
a bunch of money to stay with him,

12:42.048 --> 12:45.074
and have sex with him
while he murders himself slowly.

12:45.184 --> 12:48.621
And, you know, she's game for it,
but she catches feelings midway through

12:48.722 --> 12:50.121
and the whole thing changes.

12:50.224 --> 12:52.249
<i>Wow, have you seen Cocktail?</i>

12:52.826 --> 12:54.760
- Yeah, yeah.
- She was in that.

12:54.862 --> 12:56.728
- She was in that.
- Yeah.

13:06.108 --> 13:08.633
- You like that?
- Yeah, it's rad.

13:08.744 --> 13:11.474
Don't talk, please.
Hang on, let me get a condom.

13:11.580 --> 13:14.948
- Brian, are you guys up?
- Stewie, what the hell are you doing?

13:15.051 --> 13:17.815
- Go back to bed.
- But I'm not tired.

13:17.921 --> 13:22.358
- And I'm lonely.
- Oh, come, get in bed with us.

13:22.459 --> 13:25.987
<i>- Oh, all right. "Dear Penthouse Forum. '"
- No, no, Stewie, go away!</i>

13:26.097 --> 13:27.792
Brian, don't be mean to him.

13:27.899 --> 13:31.027
Yes, Brian, if you're mean to me,
I'll stop paying the rent.

13:31.135 --> 13:33.433
- What did he say?
- Nothing.

13:33.538 --> 13:37.202
That's right, I'm paying
Mr. Lickity Self's half of the rent.

13:37.309 --> 13:38.606
Is that true?

13:38.710 --> 13:42.669
- All right, yes, fine, it's true.
- Why didn't you say anything?

13:42.781 --> 13:45.250
Because you wanted me
to move in so badly,

13:45.351 --> 13:47.046
and God knows I didn't want to...

13:47.153 --> 13:50.384
Wait... You didn't want to
move in with me?

13:50.490 --> 13:52.549
Well, honestly, no.

13:52.659 --> 13:56.391
Oh, my God! I've never felt so stupid!

13:56.497 --> 13:57.486
- Really?
- Really?

13:57.598 --> 13:59.930
Well, I don't want to be
your guilty burden, Brian!

14:00.034 --> 14:03.402
- We're through!
- Jillian, wait!

14:03.505 --> 14:05.666
- Damn it.
- I'm sorry, Brian.

14:05.774 --> 14:07.207
You'll feel better in the morning.

14:09.678 --> 14:11.669
Hey, you know
what you should do?

14:11.780 --> 14:13.112
You should have sex with somebody else

14:13.216 --> 14:15.309
just to get back at her
for walking out on you.

14:15.418 --> 14:18.910
Just have sex with somebody. Anybody.
Just don't even think about it.

14:19.021 --> 14:21.956
The next person you see.
The very next person you see.

14:31.603 --> 14:35.733
- She's gone, Jillian's gone.
- Look, Brian, I know you're upset now,

14:35.840 --> 14:38.673
but I think it's important
to see things in perspective.

14:38.776 --> 14:42.235
Remember when Alex P. Keaton
lost his girlfriend?

14:42.348 --> 14:45.613
And then he got another one,
and everything was all right?

14:45.718 --> 14:48.778
And then he got Parkinson's. Yikes.

14:48.888 --> 14:52.950
You know, Stewie, you're right.
This is not a loss, it's an opportunity.

14:53.059 --> 14:55.892
I'm free now.
I've got my own place, no attachments.

14:55.996 --> 15:00.126
There you are. That's just the kind of
can-do spirit that built this nation.

15:00.367 --> 15:03.030
"We hold these truths to be self-evident,

15:03.137 --> 15:06.402
- "that all men are created equal."
- Except the Jews.

15:06.507 --> 15:09.999
Franklin, for the fifth time,
I'm sorry you overpaid for your house,

15:10.112 --> 15:12.512
- but it's not going in.
- You'll be sorry.

15:12.614 --> 15:14.013
Noted. Moving on.

15:17.019 --> 15:22.083
- So, Meg, any luck finding another job?
- No. Hardly anybody's hiring right now.

15:22.191 --> 15:25.752
The only job I could find was
for a phone sex line, and I sucked at it.

15:26.029 --> 15:32.060
What am I wearing? A hat and glasses.

15:32.903 --> 15:36.839
What kind of underwear? I don't know.

15:36.941 --> 15:40.400
Big underwear, I guess. I'm sorry, what?

15:40.679 --> 15:44.137
Oh, what would I do to you? Well...

15:44.649 --> 15:49.883
<i>I guess maybe we'd get pizza.
And we could watch House.</i>

15:49.989 --> 15:51.513
All right, I am totally flaccid,

15:51.624 --> 15:54.058
but thank you anyway, ma'am,
I appreciated your time.

15:54.293 --> 15:55.783
Mom, check it out!

15:55.895 --> 16:00.299
I just got my paycheck and my salary's
doubled ever since Meg got fired.

16:00.400 --> 16:02.265
Oh, shut up, you bastard!

16:02.936 --> 16:07.100
Chris, we should have a talk about Meg.
She's really upset that she got fired.

16:07.207 --> 16:10.177
Gee, I didn't realize working at the store
meant that much to her.

16:10.278 --> 16:13.907
You know, it would mean the world to her
if she could get her job back.

16:14.015 --> 16:17.041
And you'd be one terrific brother
if you could help her.

16:17.151 --> 16:20.315
Well, gosh, Mom, I'll sure try. Poor Meg.

16:20.422 --> 16:24.620
She got a worse deal than that no-armed
baseball player, Bucky LaGrange.

16:25.761 --> 16:28.128
<i>Groundball to shortstop.
The throw is to second,</i>

16:28.231 --> 16:32.463
<i>and again, the ball sails past LaGrange
into right field.</i>

16:32.569 --> 16:37.200
<i>The runners will score and a cascade
of '"boos '"rain down from the stands,</i>

16:37.308 --> 16:42.405
<i>as clearly the fans' sympathy for this
scrappy, little no-armed man has run out.</i>

16:42.546 --> 16:44.741
<i>Now, granted, the throw was a little wide,</i>

16:44.849 --> 16:48.013
<i>but you've got to believe that a two-armed
player would've made the catch.</i>

16:48.120 --> 16:51.385
<i>In fact, a one-armed player
would have at least had a shot at it,</i>

16:51.490 --> 16:54.118
<i>which calls to mind
the question once again,</i>

16:54.226 --> 16:57.685
<i>why, with all the two-armed youngsters
waiting in the minor leagues,</i>

16:57.797 --> 17:00.288
<i>does this team stick with
an armless second baseman?</i>

17:00.400 --> 17:05.099
<i>- And he hasn't had a hit in ever.
- In ever, Jerry. In ever.</i>

17:11.578 --> 17:14.046
What the hell? What are you people doing
in my apartment?

17:14.148 --> 17:16.811
Hey! You made it.

17:16.918 --> 17:20.115
- What is all this? What's going on?
- You, that's what's going on.

17:20.221 --> 17:21.950
Come on, time for you
to meet some women

17:22.057 --> 17:24.583
who are gonna make you
forget about Jillian.

17:24.693 --> 17:28.720
- Looks like there's a lot of gay guys here.
- Yeah, everybody's having a good time.

17:28.831 --> 17:31.129
Brian, I want to introduce you to Joanna.

17:31.233 --> 17:35.830
- Look out for this one, she's a bit of a card.
- Okay, here's one for you.

17:35.939 --> 17:40.808
- What food can't make up its mind?
- This is gonna be good.

17:42.446 --> 17:44.176
A waffle.

17:49.787 --> 17:53.815
This one. Didn't I warn you, right? Right?

17:58.263 --> 17:59.252
How are you still single?

18:03.603 --> 18:06.037
Hey there, buddy. Check it out.
Check it out.

18:06.139 --> 18:09.836
I put a cruller in the Jerry's Kids jar.
I thought that would be funny.

18:09.943 --> 18:14.108
That is hilarious, but, Carl,
I want you to hire my sister back.

18:14.215 --> 18:17.446
No, Chris, she's a pain in the ass.
I don't want her back in here.

18:17.551 --> 18:22.079
<i>Well, that's a shame, because
I watched Event Horizon last night.</i>

18:22.190 --> 18:27.184
- No way! We have to talk about it!
- Yeah, well, my memory is kind of hazy.

18:27.295 --> 18:29.923
We have to talk about every scene, man.

18:30.031 --> 18:33.934
Hey, hey, hey! Remember when
Jack Noseworthy's eyes explode?

18:34.036 --> 18:37.472
Wasn't that awesome? Please agree
with me that, that was awesome.

18:37.573 --> 18:40.474
Well, if you hire Meg back,
maybe I'll have an opinion.

18:40.576 --> 18:43.740
She's hired, she's hired!
What do you think of it?

18:43.847 --> 18:45.109
It was awesome!

18:45.215 --> 18:47.706
- Wasn't it awesome?
- It was totally awesome!

18:47.818 --> 18:51.277
It was the most awesome thing ever!
Hug me!

18:54.659 --> 18:56.957
- Hey, how you doing, Brian?
- Lousy.

18:57.061 --> 19:01.556
<i>I know who can cheer you up.
The robot from SpaceCamp.</i>

19:01.667 --> 19:05.728
- Brian and Jinx are friends.
- Get that out of here.

19:05.838 --> 19:09.296
<i>Okay, how about the robot from Rocky IV?</i>

19:20.955 --> 19:24.721
Look, Stewie, get these stupid '80s movie
robots out of here, and leave me alone.

19:24.825 --> 19:26.588
It's all your fault that Jillian's gone.

19:26.694 --> 19:30.495
My fault? Brian, you've got
no one to blame but yourself.

19:30.599 --> 19:32.499
You let the fat man talk you
into moving out.

19:32.601 --> 19:35.866
You let Jillian walk out the door.
Stop getting pushed around.

19:35.971 --> 19:38.769
Be a man. If you want her, go get her.

19:38.874 --> 19:41.207
You know something?
You are absolutely right.

19:41.311 --> 19:44.940
It is time for me
to take charge of my own life.

19:45.048 --> 19:48.506
Stand aside, I got to get my girl back.

19:49.587 --> 19:51.214
Go, get her, Brian.

20:05.270 --> 20:07.670
- Hi.
- Hi, Brian.

20:07.772 --> 20:12.574
- What are you doing here?
- Jillian, look, I made a huge mistake.

20:12.678 --> 20:14.202
I don't want to lose you.

20:14.313 --> 20:18.648
You know, you really hurt me, Brian.
And I can't let you do that again.

20:18.752 --> 20:20.549
Look, I won't. I promise.

20:20.654 --> 20:25.318
I don't know how to tell you this,
but you're too late. I met someone else.

20:25.425 --> 20:30.762
<i>Jillian, do you get the Oxygen Network?
If I miss my Moesha, I get a bit crabby.</i>

20:30.865 --> 20:32.492
In a minute, Adam.

20:33.635 --> 20:36.536
Well, I guess this is good-bye.

20:36.639 --> 20:39.938
- Please don't send me away.
- I have to.

20:40.042 --> 20:41.737
You broke my heart.

21:03.267 --> 21:05.759
Well, Meg, you got your job back.

21:05.871 --> 21:09.329
Actually, Chris, I don't.
I really appreciate what you did for me,

21:09.441 --> 21:12.604
but I can't work for that guy anymore.
He's a freak.

21:12.711 --> 21:14.770
The important thing is
that you stood up for me,

21:14.880 --> 21:16.348
and I won't forget it.

21:16.449 --> 21:20.044
Oh, Brian, I know you miss Jillian,
but it is good to have you back.

21:20.153 --> 21:21.450
Kind of sucks though.

21:21.554 --> 21:24.718
I mean, you are never gonna find a chick
that hot again.

21:24.825 --> 21:26.690
You know what the mistake was,
moving in together.

21:26.794 --> 21:29.422
Well, it's just another
life experience, I guess.

21:29.530 --> 21:30.622
Hey, and look on the bright side.

21:30.731 --> 21:31.755
Maybe you got
another chapter for your book.

21:36.561 --> 21:38.927
Oh, yeah, pile it on, pile it on.

21:39.030 --> 21:41.123
Welcome home, asshole!

21:41.124 --> 22:42.124
Thank you for watching «Family Guy» on
www.FOX-fan.ru